{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/769528-the-elemental-dragons-and-what-happens-when-you-kill-them","id":769528,"title":"The Elemental Dragons and What Happens When You Kill Them?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Exalted","Dragon-Blooded"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-11-19T14:03:31-08:00","id":769528,"title":"The Elemental Dragons and What Happens When You Kill Them?","content":"So, someone/thing decides its a good idea to kill an Elemental Dragon, and oops! They succeed. What on Creation happens next?<br /> <br /> Are the Elemental Dragons tied so much to Creation that Creation being to unravel to a degree? What about the Earth Dragon? Would the Wyld slowly start creeping in more and more? I could see massive earthquakes, tornadoes and hurricanes, volanoes erupting after the appropriate Dragon died but what else? Can a Greater Elemental Dragon take its place? What of the lesser elementals?<br /> <br /> I would generally say that while natural disasters would increase and life for mortal would get even worse, I don't necessarily see Creation unraveling without them. Since the lesser elementals in 2E weren't tied to the Elemental Dragons I would say they wouldn't be effected in an existential sense although I am sure the loss would be deeply felt and all would know regardless of where they were. I would imagine with an appropriate sorcery working or maybe with some loom magick one could tie a Greater Elemental Dragon to the Pole and take its place. What are your thoughts?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/687-cydoc","name":"Cydoc","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"126"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-19T14:05:58-08:00","id":769530,"title":"","content":"I imagine that there'd be a lot of elemental chaos due to inbalance, but my theory is that the Elemental forces of Creation would rebalance, and a new Dragon would respawn. If you managed to kill The Fire Dragon, the South would get colder for a bit and all across Creation fires would flicker somewhat. Forges would be cooler, torches would be dimmer, campfires would be harder to start...<br /> <br /> But then a week or so later it would all fix itself when a new Fire Dragon ignites.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Disclaimer: In favor of fun and enjoyment, but may speak up to warn you that you're gonna step on a metaphorical land mine","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2142-kyman201","name":"Kyman201","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2142_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4086"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-19T14:10:08-08:00","id":769532,"title":"","content":"Chaos.<br /> <br /> Not the pure chaos of the Wyld, or the chaos of elemental imbalance. Political chaos. If an Elemental Dragon dies, the elemental pole they oversaw is rudderless, and every petty divinity would be fighting for the position. It doesn't matter whether they can handle it, but they would want to fill the position because it has a lot of benefits. Since Gaia can't just go ahead and birth a new child (especially since she is so far away from Creation proper), it would be a very exciting time for those involved.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;From now on, instead of saying 'half-assed', I will use 'muled'. 'This is a muled job, Chris', I will say to my friend Chris. 'You need to do better, or your ass is grass. And not, like, metaphorical grass. There are weeds growing in there as we speak.'<br /> <br /> &quot;'The DEA is after you, man' I will tell him, in all seriousness.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8891-khantalas","name":"Khantalas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8891_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"899"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-19T14:13:54-08:00","id":769537,"title":"","content":"Return of the Scarlet Empress addresses this for 2E.<br /> <br /> Essentially:<br /> 1) The 5EDs are a source, but not the only source, of elemental energy in Creation. <br /> 1a) Their deaths would remove some, but not all, of that energy. <br /> 2) Gaia could create a replacement for one of her dead children.<br /> 2a) Probably by elevating a Dragonblood. But to answer your question, I see a Lesser Dragon getting elevated, but Greater Dragons are insane (probably not a good idea to give them more power).<br /> 3) You don't kill an Elemental Dragon without serious, Sword of Creation, level firepower.<br /> 3a) And if you are using the Realm Defence Grid, you've probably just nuked an elemental pole as well.<br /> 3b) Nuking the elemental pole of Earth will, indeed, cause the Wyld to seep in and Creation to unravel.<br /> <br /> For 3E... I have no idea. Whatever fits the story, I guess.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/899114-the-official-exalted-forum-introduction-thread?p=899399#post899399\" target=\"_blank\">Hi, I'm JohnDoe244</a>. My posts represent my opinions, not facts.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/531-johndoe244","name":"JohnDoe244","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar531_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2958"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-19T14:39:00-08:00","id":769555,"title":"","content":"The death of one of the elemental dragons would seriously unbalance the vital Snakes/Spiders dichotomy upon which the essential meta-structure of Creation rests. The death of two would court a spider apocalypse.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":11}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/789-mercury","name":"Mercury","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar789_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"234"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-19T14:55:12-08:00","id":769571,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mercury</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/769528-the-elemental-dragons-and-what-happens-when-you-kill-them?p=769555#post769555\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The death of one of the elemental dragons would seriously unbalance the vital Snakes/Spiders dichotomy upon which the essential meta-structure of Creation rests. The death of two would court a spider apocalypse.</div> </div> </div> </div>Sounds hilariously terrifying!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/687-cydoc","name":"Cydoc","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"126"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-19T15:11:53-08:00","id":769588,"title":"","content":"Let's say you kill the Great Dragon of Water.<br /> <br /> In the moment of her death, you are destroyed by her surging blood. When she falls to the ground, her Essence seeps into the dragon lines, overwhelming them. The Essence of Water surges across Creation, driving up the tide and reviving dead rivers. The immediate environs of her death are annihilated, while the rest of Creation knows a sudden and untimely Season of Water. For three months, rain falls even on the Pole of Fire.<br /> <br /> The next year, there is no Season of Water, only cold and unseasonal drought. So also the year after, and the year after that (though each drought is less severe than the last). Only four years after the death of Water does the cycle of seasons and elements return to normal, when the fallen Dragon is reincarnated at the heart of the Pole of Water.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":8}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/97-the-mg","name":"The MG","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar97_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2460"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-19T20:38:55-08:00","id":769739,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mercury</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/769528-the-elemental-dragons-and-what-happens-when-you-kill-them?p=769555#post769555\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The death of one of the elemental dragons would seriously unbalance the vital Snakes/Spiders dichotomy upon which the essential meta-structure of Creation rests. The death of two would court a spider apocalypse.</div> </div> </div> </div><img src=\"http://mlpforums.com/uploads/post_images/img-3100012-1-evil_spider.jpg\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/><br /> <br /> Just as planned...<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kyman201</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/769528-the-elemental-dragons-and-what-happens-when-you-kill-them?p=769530#post769530\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But then a week or so later it would all fix itself when a new Fire Dragon ignites.</div> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The MG</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/769528-the-elemental-dragons-and-what-happens-when-you-kill-them?p=769588#post769588\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Only four years after the death of Water does the cycle of seasons and elements return to normal, when the fallen Dragon is reincarnated at the heart of the Pole of Water.</div> </div> </div> </div>I feel as though killing off an Elemental Dragon is too big of an event for the the ST to say &quot;In a week/four years, everything returns to normal.&quot; It should be one of those things where Creation is forever altered, probably in a severe way.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Come and rock me Amadeus.","edited":{"userid":296,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/296-hippokrene","user":"hippokrene","date":". 11-19-2015, 11:42 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/296-hippokrene","name":"hippokrene","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar296_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2399"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-19T22:12:57-08:00","id":769768,"title":"","content":"I like The MG's idea, except I agree with Hippokrene that it wouldn't go back to normal. The elemental imbalance would continue screwing things up until Gaia transforms a Lesser Elemental Dragon or Dragon-Blooded into a new Elemental Dragon. And even after Creation would be <i><b>different</b></i> and probably more broken than before.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"left\"><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">She/Her. I am literal-minded and write literally. If I don't say something explicitly, please never assume I implied it. The only exception is if I try to make a joke.</span></span></span></div> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">My point of view may be different from yours but is equally valid.</span></span></span><br /> <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/1x1ycoxJF0G9niMt5D3Pp7owZ7tw8AJvL?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted-cWoD-ArM url mega-library</a>. Exalted <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/663334-random-name-generator\" target=\"_blank\">name-generators</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/896-erinys","name":"Erinys","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar896_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4235"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-19T23:32:37-08:00","id":769794,"title":"","content":"This is lore from Ex2 and I'm cribbing from memory, so take from that what you will, but I believe that there was a bit of setting lore that said originally there weren't countless legions of elemental, there were only the five great elemental dragons. The Primordials feared them like they feared no other beings, so they slew them - and when they died all of the magic and essence that made up their beings was scattered and spread out across Creation and gave rise to all the many elementals that exist now. If you didn't want to make a elemental dragon's death kick off an creation wide collapse and doom, you could &quot;just&quot; have scores and scores of elementals be birthed from the sudden overload of elemental essence that floods through creation. That would have it's own problems that would have to be addressed since millions of magic using elemental beings suddenly springing into existence is going to make Creation a whole lot more dangerous and it will throw the Elemental Courts madly out of balance and send Heaven into crisis control mode (not that it wouldn't be there with the death of one of the elemental dragons <i>anyway</i>).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9258-col","name":"CoL","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9258_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"278"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-20T01:34:20-08:00","id":769813,"title":"","content":"I suppose it's actually an interesting question: does that personality of the elemental have any bearing on how the element it represents manifests?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/46-oramus","name":"Oramus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar46_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"277"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-20T08:44:36-08:00","id":770035,"title":"","content":"CoL, that's the origin of elementals as described in both Games of Divinity and I think the 2E core, although you've misremembered some. (It's also reputedly been dropped entirely from 3E.)<br /> <br /> Gaia made her Five Elemental Dragons, then the gods in imitation made five non-draconic Great Elementals to serve them and manage the flows and balance of elemental essence. The Primordials destroyed them in the War to prevent the gods from using them as weapons, and their deaths sent major earthquakes, wildfires, floods, tornados, and [Wood-related disaster I can't remember -- poison floods?] all over Creation. Elementals were born from their scattered Essence. After the War the Five Elemental Dragons designed and organized the Terrestrial Bureaucracy, but they've spent most of their time sleeping in the dragon-lines since then (where they probably have to stay to manage and control the Essence flow).<br /> <br /> In my headcanon they have never come out after the Contagion and Balorian Crusade to rebuild the Terrestrial Bureaucracy because ever since then, they've been far too busy desperately trying to hold together Creation's disintegrating dragon lines, and if they step away for even a year the Essence would spiral further out of balance and more of Creation would be ruined.<br /> <br /> So if one died, I imagine a lot of &quot;natural&quot; disasters would kill a lot of people, followed by the birth of several new elemental species.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"left\"><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">She/Her. I am literal-minded and write literally. If I don't say something explicitly, please never assume I implied it. The only exception is if I try to make a joke.</span></span></span></div> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">My point of view may be different from yours but is equally valid.</span></span></span><br /> <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/1x1ycoxJF0G9niMt5D3Pp7owZ7tw8AJvL?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted-cWoD-ArM url mega-library</a>. Exalted <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/663334-random-name-generator\" target=\"_blank\">name-generators</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/896-erinys","name":"Erinys","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar896_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4235"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-28T08:22:39-08:00","id":776032,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JohnDoe244</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/769528-the-elemental-dragons-and-what-happens-when-you-kill-them?p=769537#post769537\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">3) You don't kill an Elemental Dragon without serious, Sword of Creation, level firepower.<br /> 3a) And if you are using the Realm Defence Grid, you've probably just nuked an elemental pole as well.<br /> 3b) Nuking the elemental pole of Earth will, indeed, cause the Wyld to seep in and Creation to unravel.</div> </div> </div> </div>I diseagree. You might need &quot;Sword of Creation level firepower&quot; but you dont have to use the &quot;Sword of Creation&quot;. Exalts killed Primordials an Elemental Dragon is more than in their power to kill. It's just and epic feat but worthy of Exalts!<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2435-prophet","name":"Prophet","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2435_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"329"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}